{"type":"text","timestamp":1778615186305,"sessionID":"ses_1e25ab633ffeTEAhtrNAfeOEJ6","part":{"id":"prt_e1db9aba4001jrUY6tzBLu2olc","messageID":"msg_e1db9913d001UfjUx5iDiA7CEx","sessionID":"ses_1e25ab633ffeTEAhtrNAfeOEJ6","type":"text","text":"I've completed the work on issue #9909. Here's a summary:\n\n### What was done\n- **Identified the correct term:** MONDO:0015912 (macrothrombocytopenia and granulocyte inclusions with or without nephritis or sensorineural hearing loss / MYH9-related disease).\n- **Added the missing \"MATINS\" synonym:** Found PMID:31384439, a 2019 review in *Clinical Kidney Journal*, which explicitly lists \"MATINS\" among the historical names for this disease. Added it as `EXACT ABBREVIATION [PMID:31384439]`.\n- **Sourced the existing \"MYH9-related disease\" synonym:** It previously had empty brackets `[]`; I added the same PMID as provenance.\n- **Added a term tracker item** linking to the GitHub issue.\n- **Retained other exact synonyms** (Epstein syndrome, Fechtner syndrome, May-Hegglin anomaly, Sebastian syndrome, etc.) per the curator's explicit decision in the issue thread, since OMIM still lists them and they correspond to previously merged MONDO terms.\n- **Validated:** Checked out the term per MONDO workflow, ran ODK normalization (`make NORM`), verified syntax with `robot convert`, and committed only `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`.\n\n### Files in the working directory\n- `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo` — committed with the curation changes.\n- `ISSUE_COMMENTS.md` — brief, polite update for the originating issue thread.\n- `PR_COMMENTS.md` — detailed rationale, checklists, and change summary for the originating PR.","time":{"start":1778615167908,"end":1778615186302}}}
